---
description: Improve and measure a transferable learning procedure, not a particular game's solution.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Learning procedure is the objective

For learning-related work in the SDK and harness:

- The objective is a shared process that learns through experience across ARC, GTA,
  Need for Speed, driving a car or bus, and other environments. A game is a test setting.
  Do not optimize a particular solution and present that as progress on this objective.
- Keep the loop shared: observe, form competing hypotheses, predict, choose a bounded
  informative action, observe its actual effect, revise/refute, retain, and test reuse.
  Same procedure does not mean identical sensors, actions, goals or learned world models.
- Adapters translate sensors, action capabilities/parameters and authoritative environment
  signals. They must not supply solution rules. Game ids may namespace observed evidence;
  they must never select a policy or inject mechanics.
- A tile lattice, palette, fixed camera, actor displacement or level counter is an optional
  model with applicability conditions, not the universal meaning of observation or control.
  Generality requires more than removing coordinates and renaming game-specific concepts.
- Label supplied priors and compiled/model-authored knowledge. Learned content must have
  attributable evidence, conditions, counterexamples and revisions. Check applicability
  when reusing it; retain useful knowledge while rebuilding environment-local state.
- Make the learning process observable: join observations and SDK operations to hypothesis
  ids/versions, decision grounds, proposed experiments, predictions, actual actions,
  effect checks, revisions and retained-knowledge retrieval/application. Preserve uncertainty.
- Measure hypotheses formed/refuted/retired; knowledge retrieved/applied/effect-confirmed;
  experiments proposed/executed; prediction coverage and accuracy; abstentions by reason;
  conditional repeated failures; and actions/time/inference to learning and refutation.
  Missing measurement is unknown, not zero. Game score is an outcome, not a learning metric.
- Distinguish learn, retain and transfer with explicit baselines. A new episode of the same
  game is not a second environment. Renaming, translation and synthetic tests establish
  only their tested invariances, not transfer to another game or to real-world driving.
- Translate a concrete failure into a domain-neutral mechanism and verify it against
  materially different cases. Report unsupported representations and vocabulary exhaustion;
  abstaining everywhere is a limitation to measure, not evidence of successful generality.
- Generic execution, budgets, confinement and tracing belong in the SDK. Sensor semantics,
  hypothesis formation, perception, experiment selection, evaluation and learning belong
  in the harness. Verify review findings against code/evidence before calling them facts.
- Preserve frozen experiments and their evidence. Ordinary refactors need appropriate tests;
  interpreted experiments retain their registration, audit and spend boundaries. Do not
  launch paid runs or claim capabilities merely because this objective is recorded.
